## 2.2.4.8

- Added a **+** menu next to the YouTube, Dailymotion and Internet Archive search bars. Paste a video link to add it to a personal queue or the Watch Party queue.
- Videos added this way fetch their details automatically so the queue can show the video title.

## 2.2.4.7

- Added Korean text support across the interface, including usernames, profiles, chat and world names in the Party Directory.
- New direct Alpha Channel signups now count toward **Accounts created** and **New registrations today** in the Discord stats.

## 2.2.4.6

- Increased the free weekly broadcast allowance and all Patreon allowances by 20%, rounded to the nearest 10 credits.
- Retired the Halloween 2026 light show entry point and closed new automatic badge unlocks. Previously earned badges stay on profiles.

## 2.2.4.5

- Create an Alpha Channel account with just a username. XIVAuth remains available at signup and can be linked later to verify your character and recover access if you change devices or lose your plugin files.
- Existing guest accounts can now use more of Alpha Channel, including profiles, friends, chat and Watch Parties. An in-plugin notice explains the change.
- Added a verified tick for XIVAuth accounts. Direct uploads in private and group chats require verification. Links, viewing shared images and profile pictures remain available.
- Broadcasting that uses allowance is available through XIVAuth verification or an eligible Patreon membership. The affected screens explain the requirement and offer both options.
- Redesigned the welcome, signup, XIVAuth and topic-selection screens. Unavailable usernames now show a message, and direct signup reserves the name when you finish choosing topics.
- Moved the friends and message counters beside volume across pages and made more space for longer usernames in the header.

## 2.2.4.4

- Fixed in-game TV rendering issues after resizing the FFXIV window.
- Added a **1080** window-size preset. It keeps the Design interface scale and lets you resize the plugin to half the usual minimum width and height.
- Improved recovery when a YouTube video loses sound during playback.
- Removed automatic Watch Party posts in Discord and the associated quick code from the Party Directory. Event posts and plugin stats continue.

## 2.2.4.3

- Fixed YouTube sign-in closing unexpectedly in Edge on some PCs.
- Improved video detection for pasted webpages. When a page’s videos need identifying, the new chooser lets you select a result, try another after a failure or try the original page.
- The chooser shows thumbnails, duration, resolution, format and audio information when available. Confirmed alternate formats of the same video are grouped together.

## 2.2.4.2

- Added a dedicated **Twitch** page. Save your channel, check when you’re live and share your stream with your Watch Party. The page also offers trending streams, popular channels and favourites.
- Popular Twitch channels stay listed after people stop watching. Channels watched in public parties appear first, then other live channels, then offline channels. Trending refreshes every 10 minutes.
- Added a **Socials** tab to profiles. Add the accounts you want to share and choose who can see them. The editor previews the icon for the selected platform.
- Made Watch Party creation consistent across pages, including the private-party option. Creating a party from Twitch opens the setup form.
- Updated **Pictionary Teams** to match regular Pictionary more closely. Fixed palette clicks and enabled word selection and **Play Again** directly on the TV.
- Fixed Watch Party kicks that appeared to do nothing, host transfers blocked by old queues and incorrect host-TV warnings for nearby viewers.
- Home search offers **Play video**, **Add to your queue** and, while in a party, **Add to Watch Party queue** for video links. Viewer submissions follow the party’s request rules, and queued links fetch video details.
- Improved YouTube startup, retry messages and audio playback. A video that fails to start now reports the failure and offers a retry.

## 2.2.4.1

- Removed the occasional Alpha Channel promotional messages from FFXIV chat.

## 2.2.4.0

- Spotify now appears as active playback in Watch Party, Media Player and Home, with the current track title.
- Broadcast Studio uses the compact Now Playing layout, with the stream artwork beside the details.
- The profile privacy popup now explains that visibility changes take effect immediately.
- Moved the **Alpha Channel** context menu below FFXIV’s standard actions and made its icon easier to see.

## 2.2.3.10

- Added a **Friends** tab to profiles. Set your list to **Friends Only**, **Everyone** or **No one**. The default is **Friends Only**, and your friend count remains visible.
- The Friends tab shows who’s online and highlights mutual friends.
- Improved loading of older direct messages to prevent skipped or repeated entries. Improved room switching, host transfers, participant lists and connection reliability.
- Fixed Patreon username colour effects resetting and improved blocking and listing visibility in the Friends directory.
- Improved YouTube channel pages with larger cards and the usual Play, favourite and queue controls. Search also retries missing view counts.
- Improved recovery from failed YouTube streams and fixed Alpha Channel context menus appearing on vendor and inventory items.
- Strengthened account, messaging and Watch Party protections and improved service handling of busy or slow connections.

